Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Doric's Quest (Falador, free-to-play) is not on the server:
Doric has no dialogue, his anvils smith for everyone, and the quest
journal entry cannot be started.

Change. New quest on OpenRune's quest framework.
- Progress is varp 31 (doricquest) through a server-only varbit: 0, 10
  started, 100 complete, the values the OSRS client and Quest Helper
  read; init checks the cache dbrow end state is 100.
- Dialogue follows the OSRS Wiki transcripts: the opening line and five
  topics, the "Start Doric's Quest?" prompt, the start with a bronze
  pickaxe, the where-to-find menu (with the extra lines below 15
  Mining), the reminder while the quest is running, and the hand-in of
  6 clay, 4 copper ore and 2 iron ore (unnoted, one transaction).
- Carrying the materials when accepting runs the coincidence lines
  ("In fact, in the exact quantities too!" only on exact counts) and the
  hand-in at once (26 July 2018 change).
- Rewards: 1 QP, 1,300 Mining XP, 180 coins, use of Doric's anvils.
  When the rewards cannot be given (completeQuest returns false, e.g. a
  full coin stack), the materials go back to the player, the quest
  stays open and the player is told "You don't have enough room for
  the reward."
- After the quest Doric says "Hello traveller, how is your metalworking
  coming along?", the player "Not too bad, Doric.", Doric "Good, the
  love of metal is a thing close to my heart." and the talk ends.
- Until the quest is done, Smith on Doric's anvils brings up Doric's
  "Hey, who said you could use that?" talk (via the npc and loc op
  overrides patch). Its menu has two options, "Sorry, would it be OK if
  I used your anvils?" and "I didn't want to use your anvils anyway.";
  the first leads to the Yes/No menu, and "Yes" runs the same start
  sequence as talking to him, so it continues to where-to-find or,
  with the materials, straight to the hand-in.
- Until the quest is done, Use on Doric's whetstone shows "You should
  probably ask before using that."
- The quest start prompt reads "Start Doric's Quest?" for names that
  end in "Quest" (as in OSRS), "Start the X quest?" otherwise.

Tests. DoricsQuestInteractionTest (13 tests, QuestTalkFixture):
accepting, declining, too few materials, the hand-in taking exactly
the materials and completing at 100 with the rewards, a full coin
stack keeping the materials and the quest open, the materials
shortcut, the after-quest talk, the anvil and whetstone claims ending
at completion, the two-option anvil menu, declining and accepting on
the anvil path (with and without the materials), and the whetstone
message.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Doric's Quest (Details, Walkthrough, Rewards,
Changes), Transcript:Doric (Before/After Doric's Quest, Attempting to
use his anvils before the quest), Transcript:Doric's Quest (all
sections, incl. Attempting to use his whetstone before the quest).
Quest Helper (varp 31 values). Cache: loc 2031 dorics_anvil, loc 10641
devious_whetstone ("Doric's Whetstone", op1 Use), quest dbrow end state.

Caveats.
- The journal text, the quest scroll item and the mesanims are not on
  the wiki (ours). The long start line is split into two boxes.
- Doric's reply on the anvil path once the quest is started ("Remember,
  I need 6 clay, 4 copper ore, and 2 iron ore.") is not on the wiki.
- The 15 Mining check in the where-to-find lines uses the base level
  (the wiki does not say base or boosted).
- The whetstone message is shown as a message box (the transcript gives
  it with no speaker); after the quest the whetstone keeps its default
  op. Using a bar or hammer on the anvils before the quest is not
  stopped. Doric does not walk over; only his chathead talks.
- "You don't have enough room for the reward." (full coin stack at the
  hand-in) is a guess at the wording.
- The anvil menu layout follows the transcript's two top-level options;
  not checked against an in-game capture.

Needs 12 (QuestTalkFixture) and the npc and loc op overrides patch.

